mode: "100644"
text: "# The PINS framework — build an evergreen traffic engine\n\nStop treating Pinterest like social media. It's a **visual search engine** where keyword-optimized,\nfresh, vertical pins **compound into evergreen traffic.** PINS is the 2026 engine: optimise for\ndiscoverability + outbound clicks, not in-the-moment engagement.\n\n## P — Position for search\n- **Keyword research first** (Pinterest Trends/Predicts, autocomplete, related pins): long-tail,\n  high-intent, **semantic** phrases. Clarity beats cleverness.\n- Put keywords in **pin title, description, board name, alt text, image file name.** Build **boards as\n  keyword-themed clusters** under one pillar at a time. (The keyword research + title/description\n  craft: `pinterest-seo`; the cross-platform discipline: `social-seo`.)\n\n## I — Images that stop + signal\n- **Vertical 2:3 (1000×1500)** — other ratios are penalized. Add a **keyword text overlay** so the pin\n  reads as a clear search result *and* stops the scroll.\n- Clean, on-brand visuals (brand-profile). **Video pins (9:16, 6–15s)** for ~2× engagement; **static\n  pins** for traffic. The pin's visual craft: `pinterest-pin-design`; rendered via `image-prompt` →\n  `ideogram`/`nano-banana`.\n\n## N — New designs, consistently\n- **Fresh is the #1 rule.** Make **3–5 visually distinct designs per destination** (not repins);\n  fresh designs drive ~90% of traffic.\n- Pin **steadily (3–10/day; 3–7 per cluster/week)**; **space ~72h between pins to the same URL**\n  (spam filter). Consistency the algorithm can anticipate beats random bursts.\n\n## S — Send traffic + sustain seasonally\n- **Link out** to a **relevant** page (not the homepage) — Pinterest is the rare platform that rewards\n  outbound links. Every pin can link now (Idea Pins are retired — one unified Pin format); **static\n  pins** remain the click workhorse.\n- **Evergreen library + seasonal waves launched 45–90 days early.** It's a **long game (3–6 months to\n  traction)** that then compounds. Read native analytics; **repeat what earns clicks.**\n\n## The Pinterest brief a request should fill\n```\nPILLAR + CLUSTER: one pillar; the keyword-themed board(s)\nKEYWORDS: long-tail/semantic from Pinterest Trends/autocomplete\nPINS: 3–5 distinct 2:3 designs per destination; title+desc+alt+filename keyworded\nFORMAT: static (traffic) / video 9:16 6–15s (engagement) — all pins link (Idea Pins retired)\nLINK: relevant destination page (not homepage)\nSCHEDULE: 3–10/day, 72h between same-URL; seasonal 45–90 days early\nMEASURE: native Pinterest Analytics (outbound clicks/saves/impressions); repeat winners\n```\n"
